 \label{sec:trigger}
-The zero-refresh result for RAPT-Evidence (Section~\ref{sec:ablation}) is
-mechanism-level rather than a tuning outcome. A relative trigger asks whether current
-accuracy has fallen by more than a margin against a decayed reference built from that
-policy's own earlier accuracy. When a regime is persistently poor rather than
-deteriorating, the reference decays toward the poor level and the gap the rule tests
-for never opens, so the trigger stays silent even though the policy is unfit.
-RAPT-Floor detected the same condition against a fixed floor and fired 7.6 refreshes
-where the relative rule fired none; that floor is stream-specific and would require
-calibration elsewhere, which is why it is presented as a mechanism to be tuned rather
-than a recommended constant.
