+\subsection{Comparison to Historical Detectors}
+Of the four historical detectors included in our study, three produced no triggers during evaluation across all three test datasets. These detectors included ADWIN, Page-Hinkley and EDMA. Each of these detectors reproduced the frozen baseline by design. In contrast, EDD fired its trigger between 38 and 39 times per test dataset. This provided the best macro-F1 for either EDD or RAPT on two test datasets: EDD generated a macro-F1 of $0.9847 \pm 0.0019$ for the campus dataset and $0.4184 \pm 0.0165$ for the Nordic Dat dataset, respectively. Additionally, EDD incurred the greatest adaptation cost ($3.98$, $6.10$ and $4.69$\,s) among all detectors included in our study. As depicted in Figure~\ref{fig:detector}, these three operating points include: 
